Follow-up to k246. `OCP::Hetzner::Picker->server_type_options(architecture => …, location => $name)` now takes an optional `location` filter. With the filter it offers only types whose locations entry for that location is available and carries no deprecation; without it, a type orderable in at least one location is offered. `ocp init` (lib/OCP/Cmd/Init.pm around line 919) still fetches the type list before the location prompt and without a location, so the picker can offer a type that cannot be ordered in the chosen location.

Done when Init asks for the location first (it already does) and then fetches the types with `location => $chosen`. A test (t/41-init-scaffold.t / t/42-hetzner-options.t pattern, fake IO from t/lib/OCPTest/HetznerIO.pm) shows that a type deprecated or unavailable only in the chosen location is not offered. Lane: ocp-apply-worker.

